{"team":"ARI","col":"#E64868","identity":"balanced","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":61.9,"adot":7.0,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Balanced Attack</h2><p><strong>Trey McBride</strong> is a genuine centerpiece, not an afterthought \u2014 <strong>28%</strong> of targets (league ~15%).</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>49%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><p>ARI throw by design. They pass <strong>+1%</strong> over expectation (league -2%) and keep firing even with a lead (45% early-down pass when ahead vs ~41%) \u2014 the kind of pass-first identity that keeps receivers live in every script.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 64% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they stay aggressive, throwing <strong>59%</strong> of the time, which puts scoring equity on <strong>Michael Wilson</strong>. And with the TE commanding 28% of targets, <strong>Trey McBride</strong> is a live red-zone option too.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 The Run Comes Free</h2><p>They surrender <strong>128 rushing</strong> and <strong>237 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against backs out of the backfield</strong> \u2014 23 rec yds/game (vs ~18). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR2s \u2014 just 30 rec yds/game (vs ~36); fade receiving props there.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 48% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.47/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>They leak <strong>TE touchdowns</strong> (0.32/game vs ~0.24) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs); <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line; <strong>opposing TE anytime-TD</strong> is a repeatable angle.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Jacoby Brissett","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":10,"props":{"Comp":22.61,"Att":35.43,"Pass Yds":235.74,"Pass TD":1.34,"INT":0.49,"Rush Yds":14.54},"d":{"completions":22.61,"attempts":35.43,"pass_yards":235.74,"pass_td":1.34,"interceptions":0.49,"rush_att":3.06,"rush_yards":14.54}}],"RB":[{"name":"Jeremiyah Love","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":29,"props":{"Rush Att":16.62,"Rush Yds":71.35,"Tgt":2.92,"Rec":2.32,"Rec Yds":16.75},"d":{"rush_att":16.62,"rush_yards":71.35,"targets":2.92,"receptions":2.32,"rec_yards":16.75,"rec_td":0.07}},{"name":"Tyler Allgeier","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":22,"props":{"Rush Att":9.06,"Rush Yds":38.16,"Tgt":2.81,"Rec":2.04,"Rec Yds":16.39},"d":{"rush_att":9.06,"rush_yards":38.16,"targets":2.81,"receptions":2.04,"rec_yards":16.39,"rec_td":0.06}},{"name":"Bam Knight","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":26,"props":{"Rush Att":9.48,"Rush Yds":33.25,"Tgt":4.49,"Rec":3.0,"Rec Yds":21.36},"d":{"rush_att":9.48,"rush_yards":33.25,"targets":4.49,"receptions":3.0,"rec_yards":21.36,"rec_td":0.09}}],"WR":[{"name":"Marvin Harrison Jr.","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":26,"props":{"Tgt":7.55,"Rec":4.33,"Rec Yds":61.59,"Rec TD":0.3},"d":{"targets":7.55,"receptions":4.33,"rec_yards":61.59,"rec_td":0.3}},{"name":"Michael Wilson","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":33,"props":{"Tgt":10.46,"Rec":6.73,"Rec Yds":86.2,"Rec TD":0.4},"d":{"targets":10.46,"receptions":6.73,"rec_yards":86.2,"rec_td":0.4}},{"name":"Kendrick Bourne","slot":"WR3","starter":true,"td":14,"props":{"Tgt":4.21,"Rec":2.6,"Rec Yds":32.72,"Rec TD":0.15},"d":{"tar